# Digital Literacy Awareness
Tools used:
To create this infographic, I utilized Canva, a versatile graphic design tool that allows for the seamless integration of custom icons and structured layouts.
The design is divided into three distinct sections to guide the reader through the concept of digital literacy.
The top section defines the term, using a lightbulb icon to represent the "enlightenment" that comes with these skills.
The middle section highlights practical tools—like note-taking and scheduling apps—essential for academic success, while the bottom section emphasizes security through "Safe Internet Practices."

About infographic:

The primary goal of the design was to transform a technical subject into something visually engaging. 
By using a consistent pastel color palette and rounded borders, the infographic maintains a friendly, non-intimidating tone.

Difficulties faced:

One thing I found particularly interesting while making this was the challenge of "visual hierarchy".
I had to carefully balance the size of the icons with the text to ensure that a viewer could understand the core message in under five seconds.
Deciding which "Safe Practice" to prioritize was difficult, but focusing on password security and personal information felt the most impactful for a modern digital environment.
